# Tool and MCP usage

Always-on rule: `mcp-triagem-obrigatoria.mdc`.

## Table — which tool to use

| Situation | Action |
|----------|------|
| Current library docs/API, syntax, official examples | **Context7** |
| PR, issues, CI, GitHub comments | **GitHub MCP** |
| Real UI, reproducing a visual bug | **Browser** (cursor-ide-browser); repeatable flow: **Playwright** |
| Bitrix24 REST, fields, methods | **b24-dev-mcp** (if configured) |
| Testing a REST or SOAP API, Postman collections | **Postman MCP** (if configured) |
| Figma design, tokens, components | **Figma MCP** (if configured) |
| Exploring a large codebase ("where is X") | Local search; **explore** subagent if it must read a lot |
| Finding a bug's cause | `lean-investigation` or `debug` skill |
| Splitting a request into steps | `staged-task` skill |
| Acceptance criteria, scope, edge cases | `feature` or `brainstorm` skill |
| Trade-offs, architecture, comparing options | `brainstorm` skill |

## Very large requests

Use the `staged-task` skill: small steps, each verified before the next. In an initialized project, the plan goes into the roadmap (`roadmap` skill).
